---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const posts = (await getCollection('blog'))
  .filter((post) => !post.data.draft && !post.data.guide)
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.date.valueOf() - a.data.date.valueOf())
  .slice(0, 3);

const guides = (await getCollection('blog'))
  .filter((post) => !post.data.draft && post.data.guide)
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.date.valueOf() - a.data.date.valueOf())
  .slice(0, 4);

const bookUrl = 'https://calendar.notion.so/meet/cameronearloliver/qc3y04oud';
---

<Layout
  title="Growth Map | Fractional COO for Owner-Led Businesses, $1M–$20M"
  description="You're probably fixing the wrong thing. Growth Map finds the one constraint actually capping your growth — from your own numbers, in two weeks — and if it's not worth more than the fee, you don't pay."
  canonicalPath="/"
>
  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden border-b border-hairline px-6 py-16 md:py-24">
    <svg
      class="pointer-events-none absolute -right-36 -top-16 h-[640px] w-[640px] text-moss opacity-45"
      viewBox="0 0 600 600"
      aria-hidden="true"
    >
      <g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" opacity="0.75">
        <path d="M300,80 C420,70 520,160 530,280 C540,400 460,520 330,530 C200,540 80,460 75,320 C70,180 180,90 300,80 Z" />
        <path d="M300,130 C390,122 470,190 478,285 C486,380 420,470 320,478 C220,486 128,420 124,310 C120,200 210,138 300,130 Z" />
        <path d="M300,180 C365,174 420,222 426,290 C432,358 385,420 312,426 C239,432 176,384 173,305 C170,226 235,186 300,180 Z" />
        <path d="M300,230 C340,226 368,254 372,295 C376,336 348,372 305,375 C262,378 226,350 224,302 C222,254 260,234 300,230 Z" />
        <circle cx="299" cy="301" r="5" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" />
      </g>
    </svg>

    <div class="relative z-10 mx-auto grid max-w-[1200px] items-center gap-12 md:grid-cols-[1.1fr_0.9fr] md:gap-14">
      <div>
        <h1 class="font-display text-4xl leading-[1.1] text-ink sm:text-5xl md:text-[58px]">
          You're fixing the <em>wrong thing.</em>
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-[48ch] text-lg leading-relaxed text-fern">
          Growth stalls for a reason you usually can't see from the inside. I find it in two weeks — in your own numbers — and if it's not worth more than my fee, you don't pay.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8">
          <a
            href={bookUrl}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="inline-block rounded-full border border-ink bg-ink px-8 py-4 text-[15px] font-semibold text-parchment transition-opacity hover:opacity-90"
          >
            Book a call
          </a>
          <p class="mt-3.5 text-sm text-fern">A 30-minute call. If I can't help, I'll tell you.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Sample scorecard (placeholder until a real anonymized one) -->
      <div class="rounded-[14px] border border-hairline bg-white/55 p-7 backdrop-blur-sm">
        <p class="mb-4 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium tracking-[0.14em] text-fern">
          SAMPLE SCORECARD
        </p>
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 py-2.5 text-[13.5px] font-medium text-fern">
          <span>Revenue vs. plan</span>
          <span class="whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-sm text-ink">104%<i class="ml-1.5 text-[11px] not-italic text-moss">&#9650;</i></span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 border-t border-dashed border-hairline py-2.5 text-[13.5px] font-medium text-fern">
          <span>Gross margin</span>
          <span class="whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-sm text-ink">41%<i class="ml-1.5 text-[11px] not-italic text-moss">&#9650;</i></span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 border-t border-dashed border-hairline py-2.5 text-[13.5px] font-medium text-fern">
          <span>Owner hours in the weeds</span>
          <span class="whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-sm text-ink">6<i class="ml-1.5 text-[11px] not-italic text-moss">&#9660;</i></span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 border-t border-dashed border-hairline py-2.5 text-[13.5px] font-medium text-fern">
          <span>Decisions waiting on the owner</span>
          <span class="whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-sm text-ink">2<i class="ml-1.5 text-[11px] not-italic text-moss">&#9660;</i></span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 border-t border-dashed border-hairline py-2.5 text-[13.5px] font-medium text-fern">
          <span>Forecast accuracy</span>
          <span class="whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-sm text-ink">92%<i class="ml-1.5 text-[11px] not-italic text-moss">&#9650;</i></span>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-3 flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 border-t border-hairline pt-3">
          <span class="font-mono text-[10px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-moss">This week's move</span>
          <span class="font-display text-right text-[14px] italic text-ink">Cut quote turnaround to 48h</span>
        </div>
        <p class="font-display mt-3 text-sm italic text-fern">
          The scorecard we build in week one — and the one move that improves it next. Your metrics, not these.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2 · THE TRAP -->
  <section class="border-b border-hairline px-6 py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[820px]">
      <p class="doc-label text-ink">The trap</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-7 text-3xl leading-tight text-ink md:text-4xl">
        The problem usually isn't the one you're working on.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-fern">
        When growth flattens, most owners push harder on what they can see — more sales pressure, another hire, a new tool. A year later you're more tired and no less stuck, because the thing actually holding you back was never the thing you were working on.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-fern">
        You're still the one every decision runs through. Good hires still bring you their problems. And nobody can tell you exactly why the number won't move.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3 · WHY YOUR DATA, NOT A WORKSHOP -->
  <section class="border-b border-hairline bg-parchment-deep px-6 py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[820px]">
      <p class="doc-label text-ink">Why this is different</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-7 text-3xl leading-tight text-ink md:text-4xl">
        Most people diagnose your business by talking to you. <em>I read your numbers.</em>
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-fern">
        The coach runs a workshop. The consultant interviews your team and leaves you a deck. I do neither. I read your actual numbers — your CRM, your books, how work gets delivered — until I understand your business well enough to own a number inside it.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-fern">
        Then I don't sell you ideas or a strategy. I do the work, alongside your team, until the thing is actually fixed and you've got your time back. I'm not here to advise you. I'm here to fix it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4 · ONE STORY (proof) -->
  <section class="border-b border-hairline px-6 py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1200px]">
      <p class="doc-label text-ink">What it looks like</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-7 text-3xl leading-tight text-ink md:text-4xl">
        One business. One constraint. One result.
      </h2>

      <!-- Case study — PLACEHOLDER -->
      <div class="mt-8 rounded-[14px] border-2 border-dashed border-moss/50 bg-white/40 p-8">
        <p class="mb-5 font-mono text-[10.5px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-rust">
          Placeholder · your real case study drops in here
        </p>
        <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
          <div>
            <p class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-moss">The business</p>
            <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-ink">$[X]M [vertical] company. Growing, but the owner was in every decision and margins were slipping.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-moss">What I found</p>
            <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-ink">Everyone assumed it was a sales problem. The data said it was [the real thing] — sitting in plain sight where no one was looking.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-moss">The result</p>
            <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-ink">[Metric] went from [X] to [Y] in [timeframe] — and the owner stopped being the bottleneck.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Quotes — PLACEHOLDER -->
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="rounded-[14px] border border-hairline bg-white/50 p-7">
          <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-[10.5px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-rust">Placeholder · real quote coming</p>
          <blockquote class="font-display text-[18px] italic leading-normal text-ink">
            "A real sentence from a real client, with their name and company under it. One honest line beats a page of polish."
          </blockquote>
          <cite class="mt-3 block font-mono text-[11px] not-italic text-fern">NAME — ROLE, COMPANY</cite>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-[14px] border border-hairline bg-white/50 p-7">
          <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-[10.5px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-rust">Placeholder · real quote coming</p>
          <blockquote class="font-display text-[18px] italic leading-normal text-ink">
            "A second quote, ideally from a different kind of business, so the range holds up."
          </blockquote>
          <cite class="mt-3 block font-mono text-[11px] not-italic text-fern">NAME — ROLE, COMPANY</cite>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-8 max-w-[70ch] text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-fern">
        Behind Growth Map: <span class="font-semibold text-ink">Cameron Oliver</span> — a decade operating inside fast-growing companies, from employee #3 to 100+, usually the person leaders called when things started breaking.
        <a href="/about" class="font-semibold text-moss transition-colors hover:text-ink">More on that →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5 · THE DIAGNOSTIC (offer) -->
  <section class="border-b border-hairline bg-parchment-deep px-6 py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1200px]">
      <p class="doc-label text-ink">Where to start</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-7 text-3xl leading-tight text-ink md:text-4xl">
        Start with a Diagnostic.
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-8 rounded-[14px] border-[1.5px] border-moss bg-white/70 p-8 md:p-10">
        <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-[1.4fr_1fr] md:gap-12">
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-[26px] text-ink">The Diagnostic</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold leading-relaxed text-ink">
              In two weeks, you'll know exactly what's capping your growth — proven from your own numbers, not a hunch.
            </p>
            <ol class="mt-5 space-y-2.5">
              <li class="flex items-baseline gap-3 text-[15px] text-ink"><span class="font-mono text-xs font-medium text-moss">1</span>You give me read-only access to your systems.</li>
              <li class="flex items-baseline gap-3 text-[15px] text-ink"><span class="font-mono text-xs font-medium text-moss">2</span>I find the one constraint doing the most damage.</li>
              <li class="flex items-baseline gap-3 text-[15px] text-ink"><span class="font-mono text-xs font-medium text-moss">3</span>You get a short written brief: what it is, what it's costing you, and the moves that fix it.</li>
            </ol>
            <p class="mt-5 text-[15.5px] font-semibold leading-relaxed text-moss">
              If I don't find something worth more than the fee, you don't pay.
            </p>
            <a
              href={bookUrl}
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="mt-6 inline-block rounded-full border border-ink bg-ink px-8 py-4 text-[15px] font-semibold text-parchment transition-opacity hover:opacity-90"
            >
              Book a call
            </a>
            <p class="mt-3 font-mono text-xs font-medium tracking-[0.1em] text-fern">TWO WEEKS · ONE FIXED FEE</p>
          </div>
          <div class="md:border-l md:border-hairline md:pl-10">
            <p class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-fern">If you want me to keep going</p>
            <div class="mt-4">
              <h4 class="font-display text-[19px] text-ink">The Build</h4>
              <p class="mt-1.5 text-[14.5px] leading-relaxed text-fern">
                90 days to install the fix the Diagnostic found. Your team runs the weekly without you by day 90, or I keep going until they do. Three at a time.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-6 border-t border-dashed border-hairline pt-6">
              <h4 class="font-display text-[19px] text-ink">Operating Partner</h4>
              <p class="mt-1.5 text-[14.5px] leading-relaxed text-fern">
                Monthly, after a Build. I stay on, run the weekly, and keep pushing the next improvement.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-7 max-w-[64ch] text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-fern">
        Every engagement is one fixed fee, quoted to the problem — not an hourly meter. You shouldn't have to make a money decision every time you need to call me.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 6 · WHO THIS IS (AND ISN'T) FOR -->
  <section class="border-b border-hairline px-6 py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1200px]">
      <p class="doc-label text-ink">Is this you?</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-7 text-3xl leading-tight text-ink md:text-4xl">
        I'm not for everyone.
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-8 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="rounded-[14px] border border-hairline bg-white/50 p-7">
          <p class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-moss">This is for you if</p>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3">
            {[
              "You own a $1–20M business and you're still the bottleneck.",
              "You'd rather hear the truth from your numbers than a pep talk.",
              "You're ready to actually change how the business runs.",
            ].map((item) => (
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink">
                <span class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-moss"></span>
                {item}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-[14px] border border-hairline bg-white/30 p-7">
          <p class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-fern">It's not for you if</p>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3">
            {[
              "You're pre-revenue and still hunting for product-market fit.",
              "You want someone to agree with you, not tell you what's wrong.",
              "You already know your constraint and just need an extra pair of hands.",
            ].map((item) => (
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-fern">
                <span class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-fern/50"></span>
                {item}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 8 · FREE GUIDES -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1200px]">
      <p class="doc-label text-ink">Free guides</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-7 text-3xl leading-tight text-ink md:text-4xl">
        Some of this you can fix yourself.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-[58ch] text-lg leading-relaxed text-fern">
        I write down how to do the things I get hired for — running a weekly that works, hiring your first ops person, getting out of the bottleneck. If one of these saves you a call, good.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8">
        {guides.map((post) => (
          <a
            href={`/blog/${post.id}`}
            class="group flex items-baseline justify-between gap-6 border-t border-hairline py-5 no-underline"
          >
            <span class="font-display text-[21px] text-ink transition-colors group-hover:text-moss">
              {post.data.title}
            </span>
            <span class="flex-shrink-0 font-mono text-xs font-medium text-moss">READ →</span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
      <a href="/blog" class="mt-6 inline-block text-[15px] font-semibold text-moss transition-colors hover:text-ink">
        All guides &amp; field notes →
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* reserved for homepage-specific tweaks */
</style>
